## 💡 Why This Works

### Problem: Pure Playwright Can't Discover
```python
# ❌ This doesn't work for unknown pages
playwright.click("the submit button")  # How to find it?
playwright.click("#submit")             # What if CSS changes?
playwright.click("button.btn-primary")  # Brittle!
```

### Solution: browser-use Discovers First
```python
# ✅ Phase 1: Discovery
state = await browser_use.browser_get_state()
# Returns: [{'type': 'button', 'text': 'Submit', 'selector': '#submit'}]

# ✅ Phase 2: Validate + Generate Stable
element = await playwright.get_element('#submit')
stable_locator = await playwright.browser_generate_locator(element)
# Returns: 'role=button[name="Submit"]'  ← Survives CSS changes!

# ✅ Phase 3: Execute (forever)
await playwright.click('role=button[name="Submit"]')
# Works even if CSS changes from #submit to .submit-btn!
```

